---
title: BBQ Pulled Pork
image: https://tastesbetterfromscratch.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/Pulled-Pork-5.jpg
cuisine: American
servings: 6
prep time: 20 minutes
cook time: 8 hours
course: Main Course
time required: 8 hours 20 minutes
source: https://tastesbetterfromscratch.com/pulled-pork/#wprm-recipe-container-28643
nutrition:
  calories: 310 kcal
  fat: 13 g
  saturated fat: 5 g
  carbohydrates: 9 g
  sugar: 7 g
  protein: 36 g
  fiber: 1 g
  sodium: 554 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
---

Trim @pork shoulder{4%lbs} of excess fat and cut into 4 pieces.

Combine @brown sugar{1%tbsp}, @chili powder{1%tbsp}, @onion powder{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @cumin{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%tsp}, and @black pepper{1%tsp} in a small bowl and rub all over the pork.

If you'd like a little sear, heat @?oil{2%tbsp} in a #Dutch oven pot{} over medium-high heat. Add the meat and sear for a few seconds on all sides.

Place pork in slow cooker and pour @coke{12%ounces}(not diet/zero, you need the sugars) around it. Cover and cook on LOW for ~{8%hours} until pork is tender and shreds easily with a fork.

Toss in @bbq sauce{1.5%cup}(generally to taste) for coating meat.